                                   "title":  "Letterboxd review of Crying Out Love in the Center of the World",
                                   "snippet":  "[Letterboxd Review of \"Crying Out Love in the Center of the World\"] This is perhaps the most gorgeously photographed film of all time, so ethereal it can’t even be expressed in words, but I will try:The past and the present connected by a box of cassettes.The past, his childhood, completely bathed in shiny, reflecting, yellow lights, as if the only thing existing in the world, apart from that seraphic girl— is the Sun; peering in from open doors, pouring in from glass windows, as a canvas to the beach and a floor for the skies. It was everything and everywhere. The present, on the other hand, perennially in rain, so blue and purple and gloomy that the Sun migh",
                                   "link":  "https://letterboxd.com/film/crying-out-love-in-the-center-of-the-world/"
                               },
                               {
                                   "title":  "Letterboxd review of Crying Out Love in the Center of the World",
                                   "snippet":  "[Letterboxd Review of \"Crying Out Love in the Center of the World\"] Damn, this film is sad. Really sad. I love films that are bleak, depressing, dark, misanthropic, whatever you want to call it when they focus on the dismal state of the world, society and people in general, but this film is just emotionally draining. Maybe it can get a little too heavy handed a few times, but for the most part it\u0027s emotional, well acted with the two protagonists developed extremely well, a gorgeous colour palette throughout and a slow burning pace that allows us to feel all the pain and heartbreak without anything being glossed over.",
                                   "link":  "https://letterboxd.com/film/crying-out-love-in-the-center-of-the-world/"
                               },
                               {
                                   "title":  "Letterboxd review of Crying Out Love in the Center of the World",
                                   "snippet":  "[Letterboxd Review of \"Crying Out Love in the Center of the World\"] \"Beginnings are just the continuations of other things.\"A certain love\u0027s uniqueness defined by how it\u0027s communicated, mortality assuaged by its mere existence and the confirmation that bond cannot truly be severed so long as remembrance tells your heart to keep beating. Physical reminders do their part a little too well, tears liable to soak your shirt as foremost \"What if?\" is mined at a depth best left unexplored, mere fortune granted by their presence remaining forever anchored as a bittersweet milestone that unlocks the specificity of your emotional register\u0027s vastness. Unition is as fated",
                                   "link":  "https://letterboxd.com/film/crying-out-love-in-the-center-of-the-world/"
                               },
                               {
                                   "title":  "Letterboxd review of Crying Out Love in the Center of the World",
                                   "snippet":  "[Letterboxd Review of \"Crying Out Love in the Center of the World\"] if anyone was up around 3 am (GMT+2) yesterday, you might have seen me give this movie 3.5, then 3.0, and then 2.5 stars. i settled on the 2.5/5 rating, but i\u0027ll be honest: i wasn\u0027t sure how to feel about this one. i think it\u0027s a good movie, with solid performances, but the plot is much too melodramatic, to the point that all the coincidences are only there to add to the melodrama, which turned me off completely. i do understand where people\u0027s emotional reviews of this film are coming from, but if i feel like a movie is begging me to feel something, i end up feeling nothing instead.",
                                   "link":  "https://letterboxd.com/film/crying-out-love-in-the-center-of-the-world/"
                               },
